# Futon – Project Rules and Conventions

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Vue 3 SFCs (Options API), Bootstrap classes
- **i18n**: `src/i18n/{en,pt}.js` – ALWAYS add new keys to ALL locales simultaneously
- **Storage**: LocalStorage via `SetStorage` service (`futon_state_v2` key)
- **Data**: YAML sets in `src/levels/`, processed by `DisciplineManager`

## Architecture
- **Services**: `src/services/` (DisciplineManager, SetStorage, SetFactory)
- **Domain**: `src/domain/` for business logic (levels.js, disciplines.js)  
- **Components**: 
  - `src/components/ui/` – reusable UI (Button, Badge, etc.)
  - `src/components/set/` – set-specific (Set, Page)
  - `src/components/discipline/` – level navigation and display

## Data Model (Set Fields)
Core persisted fields: `attempts`, `lastScore`, `gradePercent`, `status`, `completed`, `durationSeconds`, `avgSecondsPerExercise`, `pages[{pageNumber, exercises[{answer}]}]`

When adding fields, update: SetFactory defaults, SetStorage serialization, and merge logic.

## Scoring & Status
- Use `src/domain/scoring.js`: `computeGradePercent()`, `computeStatus()`
- UI shows: ○ Mastery (green), △ Pass (amber), × Retry (red)
- Speed gauge: `width = 100 * (1 - s / (maxS * 2))`

## Coding Standards
- 2-space indent, DRY code, ≤120 cols for one-liners
- Comments only for non-obvious code
- UI text via `$t('key')` – no hardcoded strings
- Computed > methods for derived state, early returns over nesting
- Explicit `.js` extensions in imports

## Key UX Patterns
- Auto-advance after page completion (except last page)
- Arrow/N/P keyboard navigation
- Timer tracks `durationSeconds` and `avgSecondsPerExercise`

## Testing (Playwright)
- Location: `tests/integration/`
- Uses system Chrome, non-headless mode
- Commands: `pnpm test`, `pnpm test:ui`, `pnpm test:debug`
- Target semantic selectors: `getByRole()`, `getByText()`, avoid CSS classes

## Development & Git
- **Server**: Don't run `pnpm dev` – server already running, ask user for address
- **Commits**: Fine-grained, focused commits with imperative messages  
- Scope prefixes: `i18n:`, `ui:`, `domain:`, `storage:`
- **Never auto-commit** – always prompt user first

## Adding New Sets
1. Create YAML in `src/levels/{subject}/{level}/`  
2. Import in discipline builder (`src/discipline/build*.js`)
3. Add i18n keys for labels
4. Run `pnpm run targets:refresh` to compute targets
5. Test persistence (save/load), scoring, and navigation

## PR Checklist
- Lint passes, no console errors
- All new i18n keys added to en.js AND pt.js
- Integration tests pass
- No hardcoded UI strings remain